course: dictionary
lesson: 3694
title: Flashy and what it hints at
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how something looks, and context tells you what that look is for. «A flashy shop next to the play button» is a clue: the shop is built to grab your eye. Flashy means bright, shiny or showy, made to attract attention.
explain: Context can also tell you when flashy means "too much". The sentence says the games are designed to make you spend, so the flashy shop is a trick. Something flashy can look amazing on the outside while having less real quality inside.
explain: Flashy can describe a person too. A boy who keeps waving his new trainers about is probably showing off. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Flashy means bright, shiny or showy, made to attract attention.
fact: Flashy can describe someone who likes to show off.
fact: «A flashy car» is a car that is bright and striking, made to be noticed.
fact: Flashy often hints that something is more show than quality.
fact: Flashier and flashiest are the comparison forms: «flashier» means more showy, and «flashiest» means the most showy.
exercise: «a flashy shop next to the play button» What does flashy mean here? | Cold to touch | Old and dusty | Plain and quiet | *Bright and showy, made to catch your eye
exercise: Which phrase means plain and simple, not showy? | Flashy clothes | *Nothing flashy | Flashiest move | A flashy car
exercise: What does flashy suggest about a boy who keeps showing off his new trainers? | *He likes to show off | He is always asleep | He is lost | He is very shy
test: Which of these is a flashy car? | *A bright red sports car with gold stripes | A quiet old tractor in a field | A wooden bicycle with a basket | A small, plain, grey van
test: Which sentence uses flashy correctly? | She whispered a flashy goodbye. | The soup was flashy and cold. | The library was flashy and full of quiet readers. | *The magician wore a flashy suit covered in sparkly sequins.
exam: Which word means bright and showy, made to attract attention? | Curt | *Flashy | Barely | Glum
